't be there  for the start of OTAs after all of the  problems he created on his way out of  Pittsburgh you would think he would be  doing everything in his power to ensure  the best possible transition to his new  team you know Mike when I wrote this  yesterday this this post about Antonio  Brown not being at the team's OTAs I'm  with you I struggle with it but I  started listing all the players who have  missed part of the offseason program or  all of the offseason program that list  is long of star players and it's getting  longer every year and I think one thing  that hasn't been talked about enough so  now we're up to two things that haven't  been talked about enough but it's that  the NFL negotiating committee has talked  about moving these OTA dates to the  start of training camp and I think  that's a really good idea I don't know  why we need the this long long offseason  guys do fine training on their own you  know make it shorter and I think that's  what we're headed toward are these days  are going to be at the start of training  camp in the next CBA  yeah but here's the concern  if you thrust guys into these OTAs and  they haven't had that break-in period  then you know I look the coaches want  more time not less time and I I  suggested that they should just go ahead  and bargain for these to be mandatory  and then we take this issue off the  table altogether and and I mean they're  already essentially mandatory even  though a lot of players are staying away  most of them do it though for  contractual reasons and I'm again I'm  fine with that  but there are certain situations where  there's Odell Beckham in Cleveland  Antonio Brown in Oakland you're trying  to get off on the right foot with a new  team and back to Derek Carr  Shareen I'm convinced if Antonio Brown  doesn't work in Oakland it's not going  to be his fault it's not gonna be John  Burton's fault it's gonna be Derek cars  fault and Derek Carr is the guy remember  that the video of Antonio Brown coming  to Derek Carr's house and they're  hugging and all this cars the guy who  should be constantly texting and calling  Antonio Brown saying buddy I need you  here every day we need to be working  together as much as we can that we're  only going to go as far as the two of us  can carry us and ultimately car is only  going to be the quarterback beyond this  year if he can get the most out of  Antonio Brown yeah no question about  that and we saw Antonio Brown show up  before actually he'd even sign orbit  actually been traded because the trade  happened before the trade deadline and  they showed up and threw at the park  there in Oakland and you thought okay  he's going to be around and be around  this team a lot and he hasn't been and I  do think that's important having said  everything I said about these OTA OTA is  moving if you're a new player and you're  coming to a new team to me you probably  need to be there to get to know your  quarterback especially at the receiver  position what he likes let him know what  you like if there is a transition period  and I think these guys need to be  working and working hard on that because  you're right  Derrick futures is tied a lot to how  Antonio Brown performs and how he gets  the ball to Antonio Brown  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

